 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The verbs the press uses to quote",
     "texto": [
      "In conversation «nói» is enough. A newspaper chooses the verb according to **how** it was said:",
      "**cho biết** = to report (neutral, the most frequent). **nói thêm** = to add.",
      "**khẳng định** = to state emphatically. **nhấn mạnh** = to stress, to underline.",
      "**cảnh báo** = to warn. **dự báo** = to forecast. **nhận định** = to assess, to give an opinion (an expert).",
      "**thừa nhận** = to admit, to acknowledge. **phủ nhận** = to deny.",
      "The source goes **before** («Theo ông A,…») or **after** («…, ông A cho biết»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The prepositions of the press",
     "texto": [
      "**nhờ (vào)** usually introduces a cause that the speaker judges favourably: «**nhờ vào** giá tăng» (thanks to the rise in price). **do** introduces a cause without that positive judgement and can appear with neutral or negative results. Context matters more than a rigid rule.",
      "**nhằm** + goal = in order to. **nhờ đó** / **qua đó** = thanks to that, by this means.",
      "**so với cùng kỳ năm ngoái** = compared with the same period last year. In a news story, always check which period and year are being compared.",
      "**đạt** + figure = to reach: «**đạt** 5 tỷ đô la». **ước tính** = is estimated. **chiếm** + percentage = to account for."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Source and date of the reading",
     "texto": [
      "Adapted teaching reading, not reproduced word for word. It summarises the 2025 figures published by the Ministry of Industry and Trade on 21 January 2026, based on Customs data: [official bulletin of the Ministry](https://moit.gov.vn/upload/2005517/fck/files/B___n_tin_Th____tr_____ng_NLTS_s____ra_ng__y_21_01_2026_f121c.pdf). The amounts are rounded; check the source if you need the exact figure."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
